'''Hina''' is a [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]] that was introduced in [[Version 8.7 Update|Version 8.7]] and can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Princess Punt Sweets Collaboration Event]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 486
|rarity = SR
|name1 = Hina
|name2 = Swordswoman Hina
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Swordswoman Hina'''  at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Hina attempts to excuse her underwhelming stats and range with a lengthy level five [[Wave Attack|wave attack]], which is longer than that of [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat]] and even its [[True Form]]. However, Crazed Gross remains a better option. Even though Hina has better cooldown, Crazed Gross has better range and 3.5x more DPS, making a stack of them stronger and more sustainable against longer-ranged enemies. Hina's wave length remains uncontested despite this and can (albeit quite slowly) chip at faraway backliners or further-back peons that Crazed Gross/Manic Macho legs may not reach. This changes when the player obtains [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Masked Grandmaster Cat]]. While Grandmaster also has higher cooldown, he boasts nearly the same range and wave length but has far greater DPS and HP as well as [[Area Attack]] and the ability to be used in 4 crown [[Legend Stages]]. Where you can use Hina, you can use Masked Grandmaster Cat with greater impact on the battle.

{{Job|Classification = Waver}}

